WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.368
Aspiration in Mexico.

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:02.002
New images

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:03.269
into CNN of a trailer

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:03.803
packed with more

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:06.573
than 129 migrants, mostly from Guatemala,

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.441
discovered in southern Mexico.

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:10.176
Temperatures there topped 110 degrees

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:11.011
this week.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:11.811
And among those

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:13.246
making that dangerous journey.

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:14.314
19 children,

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:14.948
they were traveling

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:16.349
without their parents.

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:17.484
And they are just part

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:18.551
a small, small part

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:19.853
of the migrant surge in Mexico.

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:21.221
Where many are waiting to cross

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:22.455
into the United States.

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:24.524
And David Culver has this special report

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:28.194
that you will see first here OUTFRONT

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.866
on the Texas-Mexico border.

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:33.333
U.S.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:34.768
law enforcement patrol

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:37.203
the tranquil waters of the Rio Grande

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:39.439
The flow of migrants here

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:40.774
slowing to a trickle

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:41.408
since title

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:45.445
42 ended in May on sidewalks in El Paso

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:47.547
that last month were covered

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:48.848
with migrants.

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:51.584
Today, only a handful camped out,

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:53.119
but travel

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:55.422
more than 500 miles south

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:57.524
into places like Mexico. City.

00:00:57.924 --> 00:01:00.226
And the numbers are rapidly rising.

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:02.796
Overwhelming for the Catholic nuns

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:05.498
who run this shelter.

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.867
Sister Maria Silva says at night

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.402
every aspect of the shelter

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:11.004
floor is normal

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:13.940
and not the end of the year.

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:16.943
Inside and outside

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:18.978
covered with the thin mattresses

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:21.881
you see stacked around us in La Frontera,

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:23.249
Del said.

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:23.750
Wow.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.119
The Mexico City,

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:28.021
which is very far from the border,

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.289
as she sees it,

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:31.524
has now become a border town.

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:34.260
But in the center of Mexico,

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.062
the migrants here spend their mornings

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:37.163
trying to get an appointment

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:37.730
with a US

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:41.101
asylum officer using the CBP one app.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.036
Getting a confirmed date.

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:44.971
That's entirely impossible for some.

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:46.873
You can tell it's it's crushing her.

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:47.540
And I said to

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.508
What are you guys going to do?

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:49.242
And they said,

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:50.677
Just wait, wait for the date.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:52.512
Maria Jose

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:55.014
Camacho and her husband and their lawyers

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:56.449
from Venezuela

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:58.651
arrived two weeks ago in Mexico

00:01:58.651 --> 00:01:59.252
with their four year

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.220
old daughter

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:03.323
living here for the past several days.

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:05.158
I don't want to go wanting to leave.

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:07.994
They feel like after ten or 42 expired,

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:08.828
that it's

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:11.598
now much more difficult to try to cross.

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:13.766
Title 42,

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:15.902
the pandemic era immigration policy

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:16.970
allowed U.S.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.471
officials to immediately

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:20.840
expel migrants who crossed illegally

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:22.675
without processing their claim

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:23.843
for asylum.

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:25.545
Those same migrants would often

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:28.148
try and try again until they got in.

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:31.351
Now, Title eight back in full effect.

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:32.952
Sure, it gives migrants

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:34.754
the right to claim asylum

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:36.756
but those who failed to qualify

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:38.992
risk being banned from entering the U.S.

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:41.861
for at least five years.

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:42.829
The result?

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:44.931
Migrants flooding into Mexico,

00:02:45.265 --> 00:02:45.865
where they then

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:47.267
wait to figure out

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:49.702
how they can get into the U.S.

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:52.138
And you can see encampments have already

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:54.107
taken up most of this

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:57.110
little square here.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:57.677
You can see along

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:58.111
the street

00:02:58.111 --> 00:03:00.213
you've got an art gallery,

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:01.614
a nice restaurant.

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:03.383
But then just turn the corner here

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:05.251
and look down the sidewalk.

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:06.819
You can see tents

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:07.453
and families

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:10.757
who have been set up for days and weeks

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:11.658
with nowhere else to go.

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:12.725
At this point,

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:15.995
we drive an hour outside Mexico City

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:17.163
where a government run

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:19.566
shelter is set up to handle the overflow.

00:03:19.933 --> 00:03:22.302
Officials tell us most here from Haiti,

00:03:23.136 --> 00:03:25.471
makeshift medical stations,

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:26.372
this little girl

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:28.474
complaining of a sore throat.

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:30.276
Her dad says she's not wanted to eat in

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:31.978
five days.

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:34.047
They pass the time doing chores

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:37.116
and playing sports.

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:37.951
Their cell phones

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:39.819
sit in a web of chargers.

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:40.620
Battery power

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.989
fuels their chances of getting an online

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:44.791
CBP appointment.

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:46.559
Eventually they move on.

00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:49.429
So you can see these folks here

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:51.297
are going to be boarding the bus.

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:51.931
They're going to go meet

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:52.932
with Mexican authorities

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:53.766
and get paperwork

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:55.768
that allows them asylum in Mexico.

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:56.169
Basically,

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:57.637
they're trying to buy more time

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:59.906
so as to then continue on their journey

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:01.274
to get closer to the U.S.

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:02.008
border,

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:03.776
eventually get an appointment with a U.S.

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:05.111
asylum officer.

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:06.746
And they hope to enter the U.S.

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:09.515
legally since title 42 expired.

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:12.418
Migrant crossings are down for now.

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:13.419
At least.

00:04:13.486 --> 00:04:15.788
We visited Eagle Pass, Texas.

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:18.091
Main Street, quiet.

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:20.560
But Texas Congressman Tony Gonzalez warns

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:21.728
what we saw

00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:23.396
building up in Mexico

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:25.531
will push north here.

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:26.866
So it's almost calm.

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:27.600
I say calm.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:28.401
There's 800

00:04:28.401 --> 00:04:29.369
apprehensions a day

00:04:29.369 --> 00:04:31.738
just in the Del Rio sector.

00:04:31.738 --> 00:04:33.139
On the other side of the Mexico

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:35.074
side, it's just building up. Building up.

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:36.542
The cartel will adapt

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:37.343
and then that will be

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:39.512
the next thing that they send over.

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:39.912
U.S.

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:41.914
border officials warn as more migrants

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:44.017
either fail to qualify for asylum

00:04:44.017 --> 00:04:45.918
or grow frustrated waiting,

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:47.287
they're turning to cartel

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:49.589
controlled smugglers to get across.

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:50.990
The congressman

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:52.892
proposing a bipartisan approach

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:54.460
to counter that.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.962
So I'm of the mindset,

00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:57.530
stop sending them down that route.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:58.631
Send them another route.

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:00.500
Work visas make sense to me.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:02.035
Remove the politics in it.

00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:02.769
Remove the

00:05:02.769 --> 00:05:03.870
you have access to vote

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:04.504
or have access

00:05:04.504 --> 00:05:06.572
to social services and say, hey,

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:07.874
do you want to have a job?

00:05:07.874 --> 00:05:09.175
We have a job for you.

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:10.910
Link up the two.

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:12.745
Go back in Mexico City,

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:14.881
we find Maria, Jose and her

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:15.848
and their daughter

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:18.418
walking a busy commercial street

00:05:18.418 --> 00:05:20.586
carrying a sign and candies

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:24.257
were a Venezuelan migrant family.

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:27.360
And we're asking for your support.

00:05:28.061 --> 00:05:29.729
They tell me they're out here

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:33.333
3 hours twice a day.

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:35.335
I said, Okay, get busy.

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:36.636
So

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:38.805
she was a nurse in Venezuela.

00:05:38.805 --> 00:05:40.473
And so doing this, resorting

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:42.342
to having to sell things,

00:05:42.342 --> 00:05:43.643
it's different, as she points out.

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:45.111
But she'd rather do this

00:05:45.111 --> 00:05:47.213
than just ask for money.

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:50.616
What's really concerning

00:05:50.616 --> 00:05:51.184
in all of this,

00:05:51.184 --> 00:05:51.651
Erin, is

00:05:51.651 --> 00:05:52.018
you have

00:05:52.018 --> 00:05:53.486
those Mexican cartel

00:05:53.486 --> 00:05:55.321
backed smugglers who see all of this,

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:56.823
this buildup of migrants

00:05:56.823 --> 00:05:57.924
as an opportunity

00:05:57.924 --> 00:05:59.125
potential business for them.

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:00.126
Now, we know they've trafficked

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:00.727
human beings

00:06:00.727 --> 00:06:02.729
through trunks of cars, through

00:06:02.729 --> 00:06:03.930
truck trailers.

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:04.764
Now, according to U.S.

00:06:04.764 --> 00:06:05.164
officials,

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:08.167
they've seen recent cases of migrants

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:11.204
being smuggled over the Pacific Ocean

00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:12.872
and in many cases swimming

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:14.440
through the Pacific Ocean at night.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:15.341
Just to get to the U.S.

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:15.608
shows you

00:06:15.608 --> 00:06:16.709
how increasingly desperate

00:06:16.709 --> 00:06:18.277
and treacherous these journeys are.

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:19.946
Yeah, the perfect words.

00:06:19.946 --> 00:06:20.146
All right.

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:21.347
Thank you very much

00:06:21.347 --> 00:06:23.082
for sharing all of that with us. David.

